Logging and auditing provide visibility into activities performed across Azure resources.

Benefits include:

* Security investigations
* Regulatory compliance
* Operational troubleshooting
* Performance analysis
* Change tracking

# Real-Life Example:
For example, administrators can review audit records to determine who modified a production virtual machine or deleted a storage account.

# Real-Life Use Case:
A real-life use case is financial institutions maintaining audit trails to satisfy regulatory requirements.

Comprehensive logging improves accountability and simplifies incident investigations.
